  "methodology": {
    "algorithm": "One shared Rust workflow: record {id:u32,label:string,payload:list<u8>}; two async host transforms; UTF-8 string/bytes copies; wrapping byte arithmetic; result<packet,string>. Domain errors are normalized by the test harness.",
    "sizes": "Optimized release -Oz, LTO, one codegen unit, same taraba allocator with default features disabled. Rollup-style single minified ESM by Rolldown. All deployed core Wasm + JS counted; Component container and declarations excluded from runtime total.",
    "performance": "Non-instrumented artifacts; 30 warmup batches, 7 samples of 20 batches. Same host Promise microtask. --no-liftoff recommended; timings are local observations, not universal guarantees.",
    "memory": "Separate measured binaries with identical counting allocator wrappers. Four timer/immediate turns before/after each batch drain deferred post-return work. Peak requested Rust heap bytes excludes allocator metadata, fragmentation, JS heap, and static storage. Linear bytes includes static pool, stack and reserved pages; monotone Wasm high-water mark. Instrumentation is excluded from reported size/timing.",
    "host": "Both run on the same Node/V8. Component uses standard Canonical ABI / JSPI via jco; Core uses private Promise ABI. Not a Wasmtime/WASI comparison.",
    "safari_browser_verified": false
  },
